>The Josephus Problem</h1></header><div class=3D"style-module-scss-module__=
ubvNPq__problemDescription"><p>There are <code>n</code> people standing in =
a circle, numbered from <code>0</code> to <code>n - 1</code>. Starting from=
 person 0, count <code>k</code> people clockwise and remove the <code>kth</=
code> person. After the removal, begin counting again from the next person =
still in the circle. Repeat this process until only one person remains, and=
 return that person's position.</p><h4 id=3D"example">Example:</h4><figure =
class=3D"py-1"><div style=3D"display:flex;justify-content:center"><img alt=
=3D"Image represents a step-by-step process demonstrating a coding pattern,=
