EjisbLnWxFQGUTRjiHGoKY1oV5c"></div></figure><pre><code class=3D"hljs langua=
ge-python">Input: n =3D <span class=3D"hljs-number">5</span>, k =3D <span c=
lass=3D"hljs-number">2</span>
Output: <span class=3D"hljs-number">2</span>
</code></pre><h4 id=3D"constraints">Constraints:</h4><ul>
<li>There will be at least one person in the circle</li>
<li><code>k</code> will at least be equal to 1.</li>
</ul></div>
<h2 id=3D"intuition">Intuition</h2>
<p>The naive approach to solving this problem is to simulate the removal of=
 people step by step. We can create a circular linked list with n nodes. St=
arting from node 0, we iterate through the linked list, removing every kth =
person. The last node remaining after all removals will represent the last =
remaining person.</p>
<p>This approach takes <span class=3D"katex"><span class=3D"katex-mathml"><=
math xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</m=
i><mo stretchy=3D"false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=E2=8B=85</mo><mi>k</mi><mo st=
retchy=3D"false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=3D"application/x-tex">O(=
n\cdot k)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=3D"katex-html" =
aria-hidden=3D"true"><span class=3D"base"><span class=3D"strut" style=3D"he=
ight:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em"></span><span class=3D"mord mathnormal" sty=
le=3D"margin-right:0.02778em">O</span><span class=3D"mopen">(</span><span c=
lass=3D"mord mathnormal">n</span><span class=3D"mspace" style=3D"margin-rig=
ht:0.2222em"></span><span class=3D"mbin">=E2=8B=85</span><span class=3D"msp=
ace" style=3D"margin-right:0.2222em"></span></span><span class=3D"base"><sp=
an class=3D"strut" style=3D"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em"></span><span=
 class=3D"mord mathnormal" style=3D"margin-right:0.03148em">k</span><span c=
lass=3D"mclose">)</span></span></span></span> time because, to remove a nod=
e, we must iterate through <span class=3D"katex"><span class=3D"katex-mathm=
l"><math xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>=
k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=3D"application/x-tex">k</annotation></sem=
antics></math></span><span class=3D"katex-html" aria-hidden=3D"true"><span =
class=3D"base"><span class=3D"strut" style=3D"height:0.6944em"></span><span=
 class=3D"mord mathnormal" style=3D"margin-right:0.03148em">k</span></span>=
</span></span> nodes in the linked list. Therefore, for each of the <span c=
lass=3D"katex"><span class=3D"katex-mathml"><math xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.or=
g/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=
=3D"application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=
